    {
      "id": "2RAy06-NMDezaS69LdI8A",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 699.4593047542454,
      "y": -1100.0826461582747,
      "width": 2033.25,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1571307564,
      "version": 1683,
      "versionNonce": 955378654,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793633689024,
      "created": 1793518418589,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A catastral reference can have many lots associated (because it may appear in subsequent rounds)\n\nA lot can have many catastral references\n\n- Catastral references and lots have a many-to-many relationship that is modeled using a junction table.\n\nA catastral reference belongs to exactly one municipio.\n\nOne municipio can have many catastral references.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A catastral reference can have many lots associated (because it may appear in subsequent rounds)\n\nA lot can have many catastral references\n\n- Catastral references and lots have a many-to-many relationship that is modeled using a junction table.\n\nA catastral reference belongs to exactly one municipio.\n\nOne municipio can have many catastral references.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
